  "description": "The bullish zigzag, run into its own last external high. One candle wicks four above the level and closes below it; the next closes one above on a smaller high. Only the second is a break.",
  "labelling_rationale": "\u00a73.5's BOS has never fired in a golden series, because it is gated on the trend state and \u00a73.4 needs external structure that no earlier dataset was long enough to produce. This series is s4-external-zigzag-turns-the-trend-bullish continued past the point where its trend turns, and then run into the level.\n\nThe zigzag is unchanged through absolute index 299. Its last external swing is the trough at 294, which confirms five candles later at 299 -- so 299 is the first candle on which the trend is BULLISH and the first on which a bullish BOS can be evaluated at all. The most recent confirmed external swing high at that point is the peak at 288, whose high is 67, and it is unconsumed.\n\nTwo candles are added, and they are the whole case.\n\nIndex 300 puts its high at 70, four above the level, and closes at 66 -- below it. \u00a73.5 is explicit that this is not a break: 'a wick-only penetration (H[i] > H[swing] but Cl[i] <= H[swing] + e) is not BOS -- it is routed to the Liquidity Engine as a sweep candidate. This single rule is the doctrine's principal false-breakout filter.' No BOS is recorded here, and that absence is the assertion.\n\nIndex 301 closes at 68, one above the level, on a candle whose high of 69 is lower than the previous candle's. That inversion is deliberate: it makes the point that \u00a73.5 reads the close and nothing else. A detector keyed on penetration depth would break at 300 and not at 301; the doctrine does the opposite.\n\nThe replay uses epsilon = 0, so the comparison is Cl > 67 exactly: 66 fails, 68 passes. The break is recorded against swing 288 at break_index 301, and the swing is marked consumed_by BOS_UP -- \u00a73.5 allows a swing to be broken at most once.\n\nThe BOS quality grade \u00a73.5 also asks for -- 'displaced vs plain' -- is not in the recorded payload at all, so this case cannot assert it. That is logged as a pending rule rather than quietly omitted.",
  "labelled_by": "drafted by Claude Opus 5 2026-08-23 from SLS 3.4/3.5; VERIFIED by developer 2026-08-23 against a rendered view of the series -- confirmed the shape (the zigzag turns where the pivots say it does), the labels, and the doctrine question the case turns on. Per-candle arithmetic was not re-derived by hand; it rests on the generator's own assertions (every leg divides evenly, the series lands on exactly 300 candles) and on all three series being built by one method.",
  "labelled_at": "2026-08-23",
